Screen2Run replication package

Original Screen2Run code and documentation are covered by the root MIT license.
That license does not relicense third-party datasets, libraries, fonts, model
outputs, or software obtained independently.

LayoutCoder-derived adapter and compatibility material retains the upstream
Apache License 2.0 in LICENSES/LayoutCoder-Apache-2.0.txt. Its upstream source
notices remain in the corresponding files. Portable paths, English comments,
and Android-specific entry points are release modifications.

Roboto font files retain their embedded copyright and license. Exact font
notices are supplied in android_harness/fonts/. Preserve these notices when
redistributing the fonts.

DCGen's upstream segmentation implementation is an external dependency rather
than bundled source. The Android adapter is supplied separately. Acquisition,
version checks, and upstream references are documented in docs/RUNTIME.md.

Input datasets are pix2code, ReDraw, and MobileViews. The package distributes
sample identifiers, screenshot hashes, extracted measurements, and derived
numeric results, not the original screenshot archives. Obtain images under
each provider's terms as described in docs/DATASETS.md. Interface text retained
inside measurements and generated XML originates from those research inputs.

Human-study numeric records use pseudonymous rater IDs. Personal metadata and
free-text responses are not included. The displayed XML files retain the code
that was rated, with its presentation-time anonymization unchanged.

Dependencies installed through package managers remain governed by their own
licenses. The Android SDK, emulator system images, Gradle distribution, model
weights, and API subscriptions are not part of this archive.
